\section{The acceptance rule}{

\code{accept = "agree"} (the default) promotes a row only when the dictionary's
EIN is the one the BMF run already held as its own top candidate. Those were
recoverable all along and the margin gate would not release them — 40.9\% of
the recoveries measured on the benchmark. The rest are a \emph{new claim} from a
reference whose labels this pipeline produced, so they go to the queue
attribute rather than into the status frame. \code{accept = "all"} promotes every
dictionary YES and is for measurement, not production; \code{accept = "none"}
annotates and promotes nothing.
